From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AltarsCN <337293323+Altars3668@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 00:44:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] winhttp: close a web socket, and fail one, the way Windows
 does.

Measured against WinHTTP on Windows with a server in the probe that
sends exactly the bytes asked of it:

- The peer's close frame closes only its side: this one can go on
  sending until it shuts down.
- Status 1005 means no status at all, so it goes out as an empty close
  frame, and an empty close frame reads back as 1005.  Only the
  statuses a close frame may carry are sent: 1000-1003, 1007-1011 and
  3000 up, 1005 without a reason.  Anything else is
  ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER; a refused shutdown still shuts this side,
  sending nothing, while a refused close leaves the socket as it was.
- Every call looks at the handle before its arguments.
- A server that breaks the protocol -- a close status no frame may
  carry, a close reason or a text message that is not UTF-8 (overlong
  forms and surrogates included, a sequence split between fragments
  allowed), a fragmented or oversized control frame, a continuation
  with nothing to continue or a message inside another, besides the
  reserved bits, opcodes and masking already refused -- fails the
  receive with ERROR_WINHTTP_INVALID_SERVER_RESPONSE and drops the
  connection.  A connection that ends is ERROR_WINHTTP_CONNECTION_ERROR
  rather than an invalid response, and a receive waiting on it reads
  nothing of no type.  Either way every later call on the socket fails
  the same way, and QueryCloseStatus has nothing to report.
- A ping's data comes back in the pong; it was neither read nor
  returned, which left its bytes in the stream to be taken for the
  next frame.
- Closing the handle cancels a synchronous receive blocked in another
  thread, with ERROR_WINHTTP_OPERATION_CANCELLED, and resets the
  connection; a WebSocketClose from another thread makes the blocked
  receive give way and reads the close frame itself.

The tests cover each of these and pass on Windows and here alike.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
(cherry picked from commit 01cd3ead457596d8f299b42ed946569349f2f7e1)

diff --git a/dlls/winhttp/net.c b/dlls/winhttp/net.c
index 05922acca00..808c0da709f 100644
--- a/dlls/winhttp/net.c
